notes: OBJ2 delivered. The pieces exist and are individually tested; the
      composition inside orchestrator.invoke() still raises NotImplementedError
      because it needs the mode branch T051 supplies. That is deliberate — the
      repair budget, the transport budget and the outcome mapping are each
      decidable now, and none of them needs the branch to be correct.
       Two decisions the phase forced, recorded as AD-010 and AD-011. The
       caller's schema is a pydantic model class, not a raw mapping — a mapping
       would need a JSON Schema validator dependency to enforce post-decode
       what pydantic already enforces. And the retry loop takes an injected
       RemainingTime callable rather than reading a clock, because TR-032 bars
       provider.py from gateway.compute where TR-028 places duration
       arithmetic; the callable is the only shape that breaks neither.
       TR-005's unsupported-keyword set is derived from the SDK's own schema
       transform rather than transcribed (OI-11). Confirmed empirically:
       minimum, maximum and minLength reach the model only as description
       prose, which is what makes the post-decode step load-bearing.
       The TR-064 __context__ defect recurred in with_transport_budget and was
       caught by T025 the same way T015 caught it in Phase 2. Closed at both
       sites; the fix is placement (raise outside the handler), not `from None`.
       Local shells need UV_NATIVE_TLS=1 exported; verify.yml sets it as job
       env. verify.yml's own change is held on this branch as its own commit —
       it is main-owned but depends on branch-owned manifest content, so it
       cannot land on main ahead of the merge.
